Watch: Daniel Sturridge brought late draw for Liverpool against Chelsea
Daniel Sturridge saved Liverpool from a Premier League loss against Chelsea with a goal in the 89th minute this Saturday at Stamford Bridge in London.
Sturridge received a submission from Jerdan Shaqiri about 27-28 metres from Chelsea's goal, while his team were trailing 1-0.
He placed the ball on his left foot, then made a precise shot towards the far corner of the goal.
The ball flew over the penalty area and headed towards the top right corner of the net.
She switched Kepa Arrizabalaga and entangled unsavedly into the net.
“I’ve tried to take a good position to master the ball, because players like Shaq are always looking in front, so I’m just trying my best to make as much time as possible for a good shot towards the goal,” Sturridge told LiverpoolFC.com.
“I saw Kanté, I pushed my ball and I just shot without much thinking.”
Chelsea took the lead 1-0 in the 25th minute after a goal by their Belgian star Eden Hazard.
The “blue” striker passed with a fifth to Matteo Kovacic, then sprinted from the middle of the pitch to Liverpool half.
Kovacic exchanged a quick double pass to the center.
Then he released a quick shot pass, which brought Hazard to a clean position in the penalty area.
Hazard outran the defenders and scored with his left foot in the far corner past Liverpool goalkeeper Alisson Becker.
Liverpool will face Napoli in the group stage of the Champions League at 15:00 this Wednesday at San Paolo Stadium in Naples, Italy.
Chelsea's next opponent will be UEFA's Europa League Videotone at 15:00 on Thursday in London.
The number of tsunami deaths in Indonesia rises to 832
The death toll following Indonesia's quake and tsunami rose to 832, as reported by the country's disaster agency early Sunday.
Numerous people are trapped among the ruins of the buildings that collapsed after the 7.5-magnitude quake that struck the country on Friday and led to waves up to 20 feet high, agency spokesman Sutopo Purvo Nugroho reported at the news conference.
The city of Palu with over 380 000 people is dotted with rubble of collapsed buildings.
Police arrested a 32-year-old man on suspicion of murder after a woman was stabbed to death
