The iconoclasm of the English civil wars was neither commissioned nor carried out by Cromwell.
Perhaps the erroneous Cromwell will be made a victim due to the actions of his forerunner Thomas in the previous century.
Cromwell's magnificent portrayal by Sir William Hamo Tornicroft is proof of opinion in the 19th century and part of historiography about a figure that many still regard as deserving of respect.
Mr. Goldsmith told The Sunday Telegraph: “Cromwell is considered by many, perhaps even more in the 19th century than today, to be the defender of parliament against external pressure, and of course in his case it is the monarchy.
