“I met my wife in this series, so in this way he gave me my future family and defined my life in the future,” he said.
Rose plays Gameit, the girl in whom Kit's character Jon Snow falls in love, in the Emmy Award-winning fantasy series.
The pair married in June 2018 at Leslie's family estate in Scotland.
HIV/Spin: China reports 14% increase in new cases
China reported a 14% jump in the number of citizens living with HIV and spins.
According to the health services, more than 820 000 people are affected in the country.
In the second quarter of 2018 alone, about 40 000 new cases were reported.
The vast majority of new cases have been triggered by sexual intercourse, marking a change compared to the past.
Traditionally, HIV spreads rapidly in some parts of China as a result of transfusion of infected blood.
However, the number of people infected with HIV in this way has been reduced to almost zero, China's health services said at a conference in Yunnan province.
However, every year the number of those living with HIV and spin in China increases by 100 000.
Transmission of HIV through sexual contact is a serious problem in the LGBT community in China.
In 1997, homosexuality was decriminalized in China, but discrimination against people in KGBT communities is widespread.
According to surveys, due to conservative values 70–90% of men who have had sexual intercourse with men end up marrying women.
Many of the cases of transmission of the diseases are due to improper protection in these relationships.
In 2003, China's government pledged to provide universal access to HIV medicines as part of an effort to address the problem.
Maxine Waters denies data leaks by Republican senators, denounces “dangerous lies” and “conspiracy theories”
U.S. Hous Secretary Maxine Waters on Saturday condemned accusations that a member of her team had posted personal information to three Republican state senators on Wikipedia's legislator pages.
The Los Angeles Democrator said the claims were made by experts and sites on the “ultra right wing.”
“Lies, lies and more disgusting lies,” Waters said in a statement on Twitter.
Published information includes the home addresses and phone numbers of U.S. Senators Lindsey Graham of South Carolina and Mike Lee and Orin Hatch, who are from Utah.
The information appeared online on Thursday, published by an unknown Capitolian person during a Senate panel hearing on allegations of immoral sexual conduct against Supreme Court candidate Brett Kavanaugh.
The leak took place after the three senators questioned Kavananau.
Conservative websites such as Gateway Pundit and RedState reported that the IP address, which identifies the source of the posts, was linked to Waters' office, and released information about a member of her team, according to Hill.
“This unfounded assertion is completely false and is an absolute lie,” Waters continued.
“The member of my team – whose identity, personal information and safety were compromised as a result of these fraudulent and false claims – is in no way responsible for leaking that information.
This unfounded assertion is completely untrue and an absolute lie.”
Waters' statement quickly sparked criticism online, including from former White House press secretary Ari Fleischer.
“There’s anger in this denial,” Fleischer tweeted.
“This suggests that she doesn’t have the temperament suitable for a member of Congress.
When someone is blamed for something they didn't do, they shouldn't get angry.
It shouldn't be defiant.
It should not call into question the motives of the accuser.
He has to be calm and balanced.”
Fleischer compared Waters' reaction to criticism from Democrats of Judge Kavanaugh, who was accused by critics of also appearing angry during Thursday's hearing.
Omar Navarro, a Republican nominee for Watzer's place in the midterm elections, also voiced his opinion on Twitter.
“Substantially, if it’s true,” he wrote.
In her statement, Waters said her office had approached the appropriate authorities and law enforcement agencies about those fraudulent allegations.
“We will make sure that the perpetrators will be uncovered,” she continued, “and that they will be held legally liable for all their actions, which are destructive and dangerous for all my team members.”
